521 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The Department of Industrial Engineering and Management hosted an inspiring session by Dr. M. K. Krishna, who was warmly welcomed by students and faculty. He began by reflecting on the discipline, achievements, and legacy of Sir M. Visvesvaraya, encouraging students to draw inspiration from his dedication to nation-building.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

522 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Dr. Krishna emphasized the value of active participation, volunteering, and hands-on learning, urging students to build strong technical and practical skills to stay industry-ready. He highlighted the growing opportunities in Industrial Engineering and Management \(IEM\) and encouraged students to take pride in their field.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

523 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(He concluded with a powerful message: \215Jobs are available in plenty, but not at your doorstep. Skills are empty.\216 The session was motivating, insightful, and a strong reminder of the importance of discipline, skill-building, and involvement.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

